4"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T19:45:02-08:00","id":1024069,"title":"","content":"Watching The First Episode of the remake, it suddenly hit me. It was so obvious all along! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <b>Angus Macguyver</b> is THE ultimate example of the Glass Walker Ragabash onscreen! <br /> The sheer ingenuity with which he can turn the most innocuous of everyday items MINUTES into James-Bond-Rivaling gadgets would put the Greatest Glass Walker Gifts to Shame! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The Richard Dean Anderson Version would be a covert/solo Ragabash Elder with some experience under his belt.<br /> <br /> The Lucas Till version would is actually not that bad example of a Pack with designated roles that compliment and back each other up.<br /> <br /> Angus Macguyver: Ragabash Operative <br /> Jack Dalton: Ahroun Backup<br /> Riley Davis: Hacker/Theurge<br /> Patricia Thornton: Philodox/Alpha<br /> <br /> Pressing Play on Episode 2 Right Now! Oh The Nostalgia Of It All! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T14:07:21-08:00","id":1026681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1007357-inspiration-for-werewolf?p=1007564#post1007564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might pop in from time to time as I remember songs but &quot;Sky&quot;, and &quot;Genocide&quot; by Ra was a big thing for me when I played Mokole:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6HcsD20HZdw\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6HcsD20HZdw\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6HcsD20HZdw\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6HcsD20HZdw </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qh59bJGdQmU\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qh59bJGdQmU\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qh59bJGdQmU\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qh59bJGdQmU </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I had to login and comment since so few people know about Ra! Sky has inspired allot of planning for a Mummy Dwar. The song <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dciIKDASIx8\" target=\"_blank\">Fallen Rock Zone</a> has inspired a mystery that my players are currently trying to work out... if they don't kill the bad guy before questioning him.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T15:13:50-08:00","id":1027321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThomasM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1007357-inspiration-for-werewolf?p=1026681#post1026681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had to login and comment since so few people know about Ra! Sky has inspired allot of planning for a Mummy Dwar. The song <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dciIKDASIx8\" target=\"_blank\">Fallen Rock Zone</a> has inspired a mystery that my players are currently trying to work out... if they don't kill the bad guy before questioning him.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've been following Ra since '02 when &quot;Do You Call My Name&quot; hit the radio. I'd be curious to read about your plot involving Fallen Rock Zone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T21:12:49-08:00","id":1027418,"title":"","content":"In the Storyteller's Section of W20, it's stated &quot;Samuel L Jackson as A Werewolf is an idea too cool to resist.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then it hit me.<br /> <br /> Even among the Garou, there would surely be Men with Male Pattern Baldness or COMPLETE Baldness.<br /> <br /> So, I wonder, if Inspector John Shaft or Director Nicholas Fury was a Garou, would he be covered in fur all-over except for a large visible patch of skin on top of his head in Crinos, Hispo and Lupus form?<br /> <br /> Oh boy, I SO Look forward to playing Jackson *roaring* <b>&quot;Do I Look Like A Bitch To You?!??!!&quot;</b> while bursting into Crinos to <i>scare</i> information out of a Pentex stooge! :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 01-06-2017, 12:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T17:58:21-08:00","id":1028357,"title":"","content":"For TV shows, I'll add in Leverage. While watching, I frequently compared Leverage to Werewolf for a couple reasons. First, each of the main characters definitely has their auspice. Second, it's great for a look at pack dynamics, in terms of, &quot;Ugh, I gotta work with THIS guy?!&quot; and yet they make it work anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12777-wakuwa","name":"Wakuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12777_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T18:36:44-08:00","id":1028367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wakuwa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1007357-inspiration-for-werewolf?p=1028357#post1028357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For TV shows, I'll add in Leverage. While watching, I frequently compared Leverage to Werewolf for a couple reasons. First, each of the main characters definitely has their auspice. Second, it's great for a look at pack dynamics, in terms of, &quot;Ugh, I gotta work with THIS guy?!&quot; and yet they make it work anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;He has a very distinctive smell.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T23:31:06-08:00","id":1030453,"title":"","content":"There was this particular song in the Onyx Path Publishing Youtube mood music playlist for Werewolf: The Wild West. I can't find it now, and I can't remember it's name, but I can't stop thinking about it's story right now.<br /> <br /> Basically, it's a classic cycle of revenge. Guy's father was murdered when he was a child, so the guy grows up filled with hatred and eventually finds the culprit. The guy kills him, but the end of the song reveals that the murderer also had a son, who has sworn vengeance himself. And on it goes...<br /> <br /> It's a simple song, but it captures the sheer stupidity and pointlessness of the Garou's rage-fueled revenge culture perfectly.<br /> <br /> (If anyone can remember the song's name, I would very much like to know it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T18:12:46-08:00","id":1034368,"title":"","content":"The movie Wer. There are a number of things going on in the background of the film that fit Werewolf rather well.<br /> <br /> In the realm of what I consider &quot;savage horror&quot;, John Carpenter's original Assault of Precinct 13. <br /> <br /> And in the area of &quot;dark animism&quot;, the remake of Evil Dead. Also, Alan Moore's run on Swamp Thing way back in the day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T08:05:36-08:00","id":1034606,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://io9.gizmodo.com/a-while-back-neil-gaiman-heard-someone-said-of-terry-p-1640193369\" target=\"_blank\">This essay by Neil Gaiman</a> makes be believe that Terry Pratchett may have been a Child of Gaia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T08:08:58-08:00","id":1034608,"title":"","content":"Watership Down- Book or movie. This is a story that in a lot of ways gives the readers an idea how to handle the natural cycle in game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T11:42:44-08:00","id":1034749,"title":"","content":"The Kakos Industries podcast can provide great inspiration for Pentex.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://itunes.apple.com/us/podcast/kakos-industries/id823315247?mt=2\" target=\"_blank\">https://itunes.apple.com/us/podcast/kakos-industries/id823315247?mt=2<br /> <br /> Just be aware, if you listen and aren't a Kakos Industries shareholder....well....you weren't using your soul for much anyway.</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/nbylxup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n77xu8p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1667-novagain","name":"Novagain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T18:54:06-08:00","id":1034996,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Jnlo_YTJ8Qc\" target=\"_blank\">Xavier Rudd, The Mother</a><br /> A less aggressive Gaian song","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T13:57:52-08:00","id":1036262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/U-ZDBddRXFA\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/U-ZDBddRXFA\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/U-ZDBddRXFA\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/U-ZDBddRXFA </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Long Way Down, Robert DeLong.<br /> <br /> This song is definitely sung by a BSD trying to corrupt a Gaian Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T15:19:05-08:00","id":1036300,"title":"","content":"Assorted creepy monster's that seem to fit well in Werewolf stuff:<br /> <br /> Splinter (2008)<br /> Primal (2010)<br /> CHUD (1984)<br /> Pumpkinhead (1988)<br /> The Descent (2005)<br /> Mimic (1997)<br /> The Relic (1997)<br /> <br /> Also, Clive Barker's short story &quot;Rawhead Rex&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T17:17:44-08:00","id":1036925,"title":"","content":"For a neat interpretation of &quot;Stepping Sideways&quot; where you exist in a parallel world where you can still see what's happening on the other side?<br /> <br /> Watch The Fight Between Goku, Vegeta and Metal Cooler in &quot;Dragonball Z: Cooler's Revenge&quot; Movie Special<br /> <br /> One particular moment, where Cooler (the villain) uses Instant-Transmission (Ie. Teleport) and leaps into a parallel dimension, completely tinted in eerie shifting red colors, to deliver a surprise killing blow on a just-knocked-down Vegeta.<br /> <br /> Now, from the Audience's Point of View, Cooler is standing over the corresponding spot in our dimension where the unconscious Vegeta is lying, but Vegeta is in FULL COLOR as opposed to red-tint because from Cooler's point of view, he is looking into OUR current dimension from the paralell realm.<br /> <br /> Goku now rushes into the teleportation realm (becoming red tinted as well) to intercept the low-blow, and both combatants shift back in full color as the former pulls the latter back into the current dimension.<br /> <br /> It's a brief 10 second moment, but an excellent reference to what &quot;Stepping Sideways&quot; would look like to one who has never played &quot;Werewolf&quot; but an avid Dragonball Z fan. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T11:44:56-08:00","id":1037328,"title":"","content":"Given the prevalence of Native American/First Nation things in Werewolf, I find the following interesting and somewhat informative.<br /> <br /> Jim Northrup's Res Road Follies, Anishinaabe Syndicated, and Rez Salute; collections of his newspaper columns and stories about Native American life and issues in the western Great Lakes area.<br /> <br /> William Saunders's Are We Having Fun Yet?, a collection of the Cherokee writer's short stories, as well as his non-fiction work, Conquest: Hernando de Soto and the Indians, 1539 - 1543.<br /> <br /> Fergus M. Bordewich's Killing the White Man's Indian, from 20 years ago, but a look at modern Native American issues and politics and how they really don't conform to the overly romanticized images and stereotypes held by most outsiders.<br /> <br /> Tony Hillerman's Leaphorn &amp; Chee novels, about two members of the Navajo Tribal Police, covering a period of about 30 years, often going into details about the cultures, beliefs and histories of the Navajo and their neighboring tribes.<br /> <br /> S. C. Gwynne's Empire of the Summer Moon, a very readable history of the Comanche and their 19th century empire in the western United States.<br /> <br /> (Saddly, both Hillerman and Northrup have passed away in the past few years.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":".  Added Conquest 01-28-2017, 09:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T16:49:44-08:00","id":1037480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1007357-inspiration-for-werewolf?p=1009345#post1009345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Film:<br /> The Howling: A news anchor investigating a serial killer ends up at an medical colony which is a sept of Ronin Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bMy favorite out of the Howling movies was Howling 3; it was the first movie I ever saw where the werewolves were the good guys. Pretty sure it was the inspiration for the Bunyip tribe.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T17:15:15-08:00","id":1040304,"title":"","content":"(Decided to make this my first post here: why not, right?)<br /> <br /> I think Werewolf is one of those games where what's useful as inspiration depends largely on your chronicle: a story about a trip to the Arcadia Gateway is very different to a story about Bane-ridden child soldiers, and both of them are perfectly acceptable stories to tell. That being said, there's some good general inspiration out there: <i>Princess Mononoke</i> is the quintessential WTA film imo, bar none; but consider also film/TV like <i>Wolf's Rain</i>, <i>Dog Soldiers</i>, <i>The Howling</i>, <i>American Horror Story</i>, <i>Stranger Things</i>, <i>The Twilight Zone</i>, <i>The X-Files</i>, etc. Children's films can be surprisingly useful: I am thinking, in particular, of <i>Song of the Sea</i>, which is great for all your Fianna aesthetic needs. <br /> <br /> For literature I suggest reading a lot of traditional Gothic tales more than straight-up horror: Lovecraft of course, as long as you understand where the pervasive xenophobic terror in it comes from (making a deliberate subversion like the recent<i> Lovecraft Country</i> perhaps more useful than the parent text these days); early ghost stories like those of M.R. James; classic works of Southern Gothic like <i>We Have Always Lived in the Castle</i> or <i>The Ballad of the Sad Cafe</i>; magical realism like Allende, Borges, Calvino, Carter (<i>The Company of Wolves</i>, anyone?), Diaz, Marquez, Rushdie. I still maintain that <i>American Gods</i> is very much a Werewolf-y work. A couple of recent collections that walk the line between American Gothic and magical realism spring to mind: <i>Falling in Love with Hominids</i> and <i>North American Lake Monsters</i>, the latter of which includes a good gory werewolf tale. <br /> <br /> Music is probably the most subjective of all, but I often have stuff playing like Nick Cave, Timber Timbre, Tom Waits, Mount Eerie (esp. 'Between Two Mysteries' and 'Sighing'), The Handsome Family, etc. while I prep. The Handsome Family is particularly good for inspiration: check out tracks like 'The White Dog', 'Birds You Cannot See' (listen to that one and tell me it's not about your friendly local urban spirits), 'Down in the Ground', 'Whitehaven', 'Sleepy', 'The Forgotten Lake'. Lots of good Umbral stuff in there besides the general aesthetic creepiness. Dead Can Dance is also fantastic; I have particular praise for their album <i>Spiritchaser</i>, particularly 'Song of the Stars', which is 100% a song for the Umbra/spirits. <br /> <br /> I also have a lot of chronicle-specific stuff. If you play in a Rage Across Australia chronicle on Friday nights, look away, you pests:<br /> <br /> Australia makes for a very interesting chronicle setting; I started using it simply because one should always stick, at first, with what one knows, but it has a unique...sense of decay that also extends to Australian film and literature. Some extremely influential pieces upon my own chronicle design include <i>Wolf Creek</i>, <i>Rabbit-Proof Fence</i>, <i>Picnic at Hanging Rock</i>, <i>The World Beneath</i>, <i>For the Term of His Natural Life</i>, <i>The Chant of Jimmie Blacksmith</i>, <i>Gould's Book of Fish</i>, <i>The Hunter</i>, <i>The Proposition </i>(an Australian Western written by that master of Australian Gothic, Nick Cave of Bad Seeds fame; I cannot recommend it enough), and non-fiction like <i>The Fatal Shore</i>, <i>The Future Eaters</i>, <i>A Secret Country</i>, and <i>Songlines, </i>all for understanding Australia's tumultuous relationship with its own past and indigenous inhabitants. The children's fiction I grew up with, like <i>The Nargun and the Stars</i> and <i>The Silver Brumby</i>, are also good for providing a sense of place.<br /> <br /> A special shout-out has to be given here to <i>The Hunter</i>, for being one of the most WTA-ish books I have read in a long time: it concerns a man employed by a shady biotechnology company, who is sent to Tasmania to track down--and kill--the last surviving thylacine so that aforementioned shady company might use its blood to craft a bioweapon (I straight-up stole this idea for my own chronicle; players have not noticed). The thylacine, in this case, is not just a thylacine but also a metaphor for environmental destruction and the innocent past of the country; the main character stands for its present state of moral decay. Good stuff. There is also a film; I recommend checking it out. <br /> <br /> Well! That got long. I look forward to making many more equally long posts in future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12920-anomalocaris","name":"anomalocaris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T17:33:53-08:00","id":1040314,"title":"","content":"First, welcome!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>anomalocaris</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1007357-inspiration-for-werewolf?p=1040304#post1040304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think Werewolf is one of those games where what's useful as inspiration depends largely on your chronicle: a story about a trip to the Arcadia Gateway is very different to a story about Bane-ridden child soldiers, and both of them are perfectly acceptable stories to tell. That being said, there's some good general inspiration out there: <i>Princess Mononoke</i> is the quintessential WTA film imo, bar none; but consider also film/TV like <i>Wolf's Rain</i>, <i>Dog Soldiers</i>, <i>The Howling</i>, <i>American Horror Story</i>, <i>Stranger Things</i>, <i>The Twilight Zone</i>, <i>The X-Files</i>, etc. Children's films can be surprisingly useful: I am thinking, in particular, of <i>Song of the Sea</i>, which is great for all your Fianna aesthetic needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haven't seen Song of the Sea, but I certainly agree with all of the others. I especially like <i>Princess Mononoke</i> for showing new players.<br /> <br /> And <i>Stranger Things</i> was a lot of fun and I remember thinking the whole way through how much it reminded me of Werewolf/the Umbra.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T01:52:34-08:00","id":1040495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1007357-inspiration-for-werewolf?p=1040314#post1040314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, welcome!<br /> <br /> Haven't seen Song of the Sea, but I certainly agree with all of the others. I especially like <i>Princess Mononoke</i> for showing new players. And <i>Stranger Things</i> was a lot of fun and I remember thinking the whole way through how much it reminded me of Werewolf/the Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Been meaning to bite the bullet and sign up for a while; God knows enough of my players are active here.<br /> <br /> <i>Song of the Sea</i> is a great little film, done by the same studio who did <i>The Secret of Kells</i>. Involves the Tuatha de Danann, Manannan mac Lir, etc. Good for a sort of 'loss of the old gods in the face of urbanisation' sorta thing; has amazing visuals. <br /> <br /> One thing I meant to add up there is the surprising utility of folk songs! A lot of traditional folk, esp. Irish and Scottish stuff, contain the grand Garou themes of worthy deaths against insurmountable odds, oppressive governments, of faith to one's ideals even when you are most certainly doomed, etc. Of course you have to ignore the ferocious nationalism they're sometimes associated with: though maybe that suits the Garou, tbh. I'm thinking particularly of songs like <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4dbFVhZ4Kvc\" target=\"_blank\">'Roddy McCorley'</a>: '<i>there was never a one of all your dead / more bravely fell in fray / than he who marches to his death / on the bridge of Toome today / true to the last, true to the last / he treads the upwards way'</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12920-anomalocaris","name":"anomalocaris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T08:55:50-08:00","id":1040700,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised no one has yet mentioned the various works of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edward_Abbey\" target=\"_blank\">Edward Abbey</a>. When I first encountered Werewolf this was immediately what sprung to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T09:42:12-08:00","id":1040723,"title":"","content":"Much of Robert E. Howard's body of work, as his stories (and poems) involve underlying themes of slowly but inevitably dying cultures and straight-forward violence vs 'civilized' corruption and dark magic. He was also friends with H. P. Lovecraft, so certain aspects of the Mythos creeps in from time to time. His Bran Mac Morn stories were very clearly a huge influence on the development of the White Howlers/Black Spiral Dancers, especially &quot;Worms of the Earth&quot;. <br /> <br /> As for the Fianna, Sharyn McCrumb's Ballad Series of novels, which draw heavily on the Celtic/Scots-Irish culture, folklore and music of the Appalachia region. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T09:16:16-08:00","id":1041304,"title":"","content":"Splinter (2008) - reminds me of a powerful manifested bane or wild fomori<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt1031280/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt1031280/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt1031280/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.imdb.com/title/tt1031280/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Monster (2016) - reminds me of a wyrm creature who is disturbed in the middle of his hunt of a gaian werewolf and turns on the people who interrupted his kill<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt3976144/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\">